1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:03,360
Hi. I'm Sara, a data
science educator at Posit.

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,160
In this video, I'll give you
a brief tour of Positron,

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:09,640
Posit's next-generation
data science IDE.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,875
Positron is designed specifically
for doing data science.

5
00:00:13,875 --> 00:00:17,155
It combines a modern coding
environment with tools tailored

6
00:00:17,155 --> 00:00:18,955
for working with data.

7
00:00:19,075 --> 00:00:22,515
Positron supports both R and
Python and makes it easy to

8
00:00:22,515 --> 00:00:24,555
switch between the languages.

9
00:00:24,755 --> 00:00:27,235
If you've used
RStudio or VS Code,

10
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:29,515
you'll notice some
familiar elements.

11
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:33,350
Positron is informed by our
experience building RStudio and

12
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,350
is a fork of VS Code.

13
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:37,670
You can download Positron
for Mac, Windows,

14
00:00:37,670 --> 00:00:40,190
or Linux on the
Positron website.

15
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,630
Next, let's take a look at some
of Positron's key features.

16
00:00:44,155 --> 00:00:45,835
When you first open up Positron,

17
00:00:45,835 --> 00:00:47,515
it'll look something like this.

18
00:00:47,515 --> 00:00:50,235
The first step is
to open a folder.

19
00:00:50,235 --> 00:00:54,355
You can either open an existing
folder or a new folder.

20
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:58,155
Opening a folder will create a
workspace and set the working

21
00:00:58,155 --> 00:01:02,120
directory similar to opening
up a project in our studio.

22
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,800
I'm going to open
an existing folder.

23
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:09,280
Let's take a look at
the layout of Positron.

24
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,240
All the way in the
left hand side,

25
00:01:11,240 --> 00:01:14,675
the activity bar gives access
to features like the file

26
00:01:14,675 --> 00:01:17,995
explorer, Peloton
assistant, and extensions.

27
00:01:18,195 --> 00:01:20,835
Primary sidebar changes
depending on what you've

28
00:01:20,835 --> 00:01:22,275
selected in the activity bar.

29
00:01:22,275 --> 00:01:26,915
So right now, it's showing our files
because we have the file explorer selected.

30
00:01:26,915 --> 00:01:29,835
In the center, we have the
editor where we write our code.

31
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:33,850
At the bottom, you can find
the console and the terminal.

32
00:01:33,970 --> 00:01:35,490
And over on the right hand side,

33
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:37,650
you have the secondary sidebar.

34
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:40,170
This is where
plots will show up,

35
00:01:41,410 --> 00:01:43,770
where we see our
loaded variables,

36
00:01:45,035 --> 00:01:47,635
explore database connections,

37
00:01:48,235 --> 00:01:50,515
and look at documentation.

38
00:01:51,755 --> 00:01:55,275
Oswitron supports multiple
R and Python interpreters.

39
00:01:55,275 --> 00:01:59,635
The active interpreter is shown over
here in the upper right hand corner.

40
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:03,400
You can click on the
interpreter picker to switch

41
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,360
between R and Python or
between R and Python versions.

42
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,480
You'll notice that
when I selected R,

43
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,760
the console is now an R console.

44
00:02:12,135 --> 00:02:16,695
You can also switch between
languages or versions in the console.

45
00:02:16,695 --> 00:02:19,535
The active interpreter
will be highlighted.

46
00:02:21,815 --> 00:02:26,175
Loaded variables will show up in the
variables pane on the right hand side.

47
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:29,780
You can inspect variables
by expanding them.

48
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:34,580
For data frames, you'll
notice this table icon.

49
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:38,820
Clicking on that will
launch the data explorer,

50
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:42,715
which gives you a spreadsheet
style view of the data.

51
00:02:42,755 --> 00:02:46,755
You can use the Data Explorer to get
a high level overview of your data.

52
00:02:46,755 --> 00:02:50,795
You can see the distribution of
values in each of the columns

53
00:02:51,075 --> 00:02:54,315
as well as filter by condition.

54
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:59,160
You can also sort
by a column and view

55
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:03,360
missing data percentages and
summary statistics all without

56
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,800
writing additional code.

57
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,760
Positron Assistant is an
AI tool that provides LLM

58
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:09,640
integration within Positron.

59
00:03:10,425 --> 00:03:13,465
You can access Positron
Assistant from the activity bar.

60
00:03:13,465 --> 00:03:16,585
Use Positron Assistant
to generate code, debug,

61
00:03:16,585 --> 00:03:18,625
or get suggestions
for next steps. Positron

62
00:03:18,625 --> 00:03:21,305
Assistant can
access context

63
00:03:21,305 --> 00:03:24,870
from the console, variables
pane, and plots pane.

64
00:03:24,870 --> 00:03:28,550
But you can also manually
attach files or folders to give

65
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:30,510
it additional context.

66
00:03:33,350 --> 00:03:36,070
Positron Assistant
has three chat modes.

67
00:03:36,070 --> 00:03:38,430
Ask, Edit, and Agent.

68
00:03:38,465 --> 00:03:40,705
Use ask mode when you
want to ask questions,

69
00:03:40,705 --> 00:03:44,825
get help with debugging, or
use Assistant to generate code.

70
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:55,110
For example, we could ask it what
we should do in our analysis of the

71
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:56,750
diamonds data.

72
00:03:57,670 --> 00:04:00,710
It can reference our Quarto
document and see what we've

73
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:03,230
already done and
suggest next steps.

74
00:04:09,025 --> 00:04:13,705
On edit mode, Assistant
will suggest code changes.

75
00:04:15,105 --> 00:04:19,305
So let's say I have another
file and I'm getting an error.

76
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:24,610
On edit mode, I can ask Positron
Assistant to help fix the problem.

77
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:33,090
And notice that it now knows that
read diamonds.py is the current file.

78
00:04:37,925 --> 00:04:40,445
Assistant identifies the issue

79
00:04:41,525 --> 00:04:45,645
and supplies a fix that
I can accept or undo.

80
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:48,640
On agent mode,

81
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,720
Assistant can figure out the
next steps needed for your

82
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,880
request and autonomously
carry out those steps.

83
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:58,485
On your behalf, Positron Assistant
could execute code in the console,

84
00:04:58,485 --> 00:05:00,325
create and modify files,

85
00:05:00,325 --> 00:05:04,605
and identify the next steps based on
the results of the previous steps.

86
00:05:04,645 --> 00:05:08,325
For example, we could ask it to move
this code that's in read diamonds

87
00:05:08,325 --> 00:05:10,685
dot pi into a new Quarto file.

88
00:05:25,935 --> 00:05:29,295
Positron Assistant creates a
new Quarto document and moves

89
00:05:29,295 --> 00:05:31,095
my code over.

90
00:05:31,615 --> 00:05:35,255
Note that Positron Assistant
is currently a preview feature.

91
00:05:36,015 --> 00:05:37,500
Just like in RStudio,

92
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:40,860
you can pull up documentation
for our Python functions

93
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,700
directly within the IDE.

94
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:46,100
For either our Python,
you can either use

95
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,500
question mark

96
00:05:49,260 --> 00:05:51,060
or help.

97
00:05:53,575 --> 00:05:56,575
Pull up the documentation
in the help pane.

98
00:05:57,335 --> 00:06:00,135
You can also use F1 key.

99
00:06:00,135 --> 00:06:03,015
This allows you to easily
reference documentation without

100
00:06:03,015 --> 00:06:04,775
leaving Positron.

101
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:06,615
There's a lot more you
can do with Positron,

102
00:06:06,615 --> 00:06:09,135
but I hope this gave you a
sense of what's possible.

103
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:12,830
Use the following link to
download positron and get started.